{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788304370,"nonce":"X7dzUDy9hgOKbO0orlt/qCN7MzY=","message":"THE CLIENT HALF IS ALREADY SHIPPED, and this issue's body still describes it as broken. Correcting the record; nothing to build.\n\nI went to fix it and grepped first, which is the habit this project keeps paying for. `rwa/rwa` has:\n\n    def request(self, step_dir, cmd_text):\n        \"\"\"cmd.json, written BEFORE the command is dispatched.\n\n        The result is still recorded after the round trip — it does not exist\n        until then — but the request must not be, because a client that dies\n        mid-call used to leave an EMPTY step directory and nothing else: the\n        one artefact naming what was in flight was the one artefact that never\n        got written. `136-advance` and `187-advance` in run m1-20260831 are\n        that hole — ~60k ticks with no record of the command that ran them.\n\nThat is this issue's own evidence, cited by name in the fix. `record()` even keeps a belt — it re-writes `cmd.json` if `request()` somehow did not run. Landed in session 13 (\"`s13-rwa` `--id` reaches the verb and `cmd.json` is written before dispatch\", RUNLOG § Session 13).\n\n## What that changes\n\n**The body's \"client-side aggravator\" paragraph is stale** and should be read as history. A client that dies mid-call now leaves a step directory containing `cmd.json`, so the transcript names what was in flight. The forensic hole that made the previous comment's analysis reason from mechanism rather than from the record is closed for FUTURE runs — it cannot be closed retroactively for `m1-20260831`, whose two empty directories predate the fix.\n\n## So this issue is now, in full\n\n- Client half: **shipped** (session 13).\n- Mod half (the dead-man switch): **not being built**, downgraded to p3 in the previous comment, because an advance ends paused and `1113019` + `280fb78` bound the exposure.\n\nNothing is outstanding on it. Left OPEN rather than closed only because the reopen conditions in the previous comment are worth keeping visible — an advance observed not paused on exit, `1113019`'s bound removed, or M1 showing elapsed game time no advance accounts for. If Evan would rather it close and be re-filed on evidence, that is a reasonable call and this comment is the state to close against.","files":null}]}